# ============================================================
# Credentials. Committing any of these leaks an account.
# ============================================================
kaggle.json
access_token
.kaggle/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.token

# ============================================================
# Data. Two reasons, and the second one is the important one:
#   1. it is far too large for git (9 GB raw, 1.1 GB cached)
#   2. APTOS is patient medical imagery under a data-use
#      agreement that does not permit redistribution, so
#      pushing it would breach the licence we accepted
# Regenerate with ./scripts/download_data.sh + src/preprocess.py
# ============================================================
data/*
!data/README.md
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# ============================================================
# Everything not for publication, in one place. The repository may
# end up public, so anything that must not be published lives here:
#   local/team.json          names and registration numbers. Personal data.
#   local/team-docs/         who owns which model, contribution log, the
#                            submitted synopsis. Attribution for grading comes
#                            from git commit authorship, not from files, so
#                            none of this needs to be in the repository.
#   local/report-tooling/    synopsis generator and page measurer. Document
#                            tooling, not project code.
#   local/course-materials/  course plan, guidelines, report template.
#                            MIT Manipal's copyright, not ours to publish.
#   local/turnitin/          similarity reports, carry submission IDs.
#   local/reference/         scratch copies and superseded drafts.
#   local/logs/              download logs.
# Nothing under src/ or scripts/ reads from local/.
# ============================================================
local/

# ============================================================
# Trained weights. Regenerate by running src/train.py.
# Commit the results/*.json metrics instead; those are small,
# diffable, and are what the comparison table is built from.
# ============================================================
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.pkl
checkpoints/

# ============================================================
# Experiment logs, if anyone adds tracking later
# ============================================================
runs/
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/
tensorboard/
*.log

# ============================================================
# Environment
# ============================================================
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ============================================================
# Editor and OS scratch
# ============================================================
.~lock.*#
~$*.doc*
~$*.xls*
*.tmp
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ============================================================
# Deliberately tracked, because this is the evidence of our work:
#   src/            model and pipeline code
#   scripts/        setup, download, report generation
#   reports/        synopsis, contribution log, generated charts
#   results/*.json  benchmark and training metrics
#   notebooks/      exploratory analysis
# ============================================================

# ============================================================
# Figures containing actual fundus photographs. The report they
# go into is submitted privately to faculty, which is fine, but
# this repository is public and these are patient images under
# the same APTOS data-use agreement that keeps data/ untracked.
# Regenerate locally with scripts/make_figures.py.
# ============================================================
reports/figures/fig1_pipeline_stages.png
reports/figures/fig2_camera_normalisation.png
reports/*_DRAFT_*.docx
